---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="home-layout">
				<div class="home-content">
					<h1>Postern - Mac Application</h1>
					<p>
						Servers as locations in Finder — browse, copy to and from, rename, and delete like any folder.
					</p>

					<p>
						Postern is a menu-bar app plus a File Provider extension. Each saved connection is a File Provider domain, so it appears in Finder's Locations sidebar as Postern - <name> (just Postern when there is only one connection), 
						is reachable at ~/Library/CloudStorage/Postern-<name>, and supports ordinary drag, copy, paste, and Trash.

						macOS composes that sidebar label from the app and the domain; the app cannot make it show only the connection name.

					</p>

					<p>
						Connections can be SFTP, FTP, WebDAV, or WebDAV over HTTPS; the type is chosen from a list when the connection is created. 
						FTP and plain WebDAV are unencrypted, so the editor warns before saving one. HTTPS uses the system trust store — a certificate that macOS does not trust will refuse to connect, 
						which is the intended behaviour.

					</p>

					<p>
						The menu-bar item is the primary way in. The app also keeps a Dock icon, because it owns windows (the connection editor and the host-key prompt) 
						and macOS offers no way to bring an agent's window forward once it slips behind another app.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	main {
		width: min(1200px, calc(100% - 2rem));
	}

	.home-layout {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(240px, 424px) minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
		align-items: start;
	}

	.home-layout img {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
	}

	.home-content {
		padding-top: 1rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.home-layout {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 2rem;
		}

		.home-layout img {
			max-width: 424px;
			margin: 0 auto;
		}

		.home-content {
			padding-top: 0;
		}
	}
</style>
